---
/** Monitoring and incidents as one block: what breaks, and what the team sees when it does. */
import Block from './Block.astro';
---

<Block
  id="incidents"
  marker="Monitoring and incidents"
  problem="Without a DevOps engineer, monitoring is the job nobody gets to."
  title="Monitoring comes with the stack. Problems come to Slack."
>
  <p>
    Logs, metrics, traces, error tracking and uptime checks are set up when you deploy. No extra vendor to wire up.
  </p>
  <p>
    Related errors, alarms and failed checks become one incident, tied to the release that caused it. Acknowledge, mute,
    resolve or roll back from Slack.
  </p>

  <figure slot="picture" class="incidents__picture">
    <img
      class="c-frame"
      src="/d/c/incident.webp"
      width="2000"
      height="1382"
      loading="lazy"
      alt="An incident in the Stacktape Console: API error rate above 5% on checkout-api production, with an AI assessment and a draft fix pull request."
    />
    <figcaption class="c-muted">
      The AI assessment and fixes run on your organization's own Anthropic, OpenAI or xAI key. Nothing is deployed
      without you.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</Block>

<style>
  .incidents__picture {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--brand-space-3);
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--brand-type-sm);
  }
</style>
